* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Generic 180 nm-class CMOS model cards for SiliconStat
*
* These are SIMPLIFIED square-law (level-1 style) cards with plausible
* 180 nm-class numbers.  They are NOT a foundry PDK, are not extracted from
* silicon, and must not be used for tape-out decisions.  They exist so that
* the statistical machinery in this project operates on physically sensible
* device behaviour.  See docs/limitations.md.
*
* Mismatch coefficients follow the Pelgrom convention used throughout this
* project:   AVT   in V*um        sigma(Vth)   = AVT   / sqrt(W_um * L_um)
*            ABETA dimensionless*um  sigma(b)/b = ABETA / sqrt(W_um * L_um)
* AVT = 3.5 mV*um and ABETA = 1 %*um are representative of a 0.18 um process.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.model NCH NMOS
+ VTO=0.45 KP=246u LAMBDA=0.08 GAMMA=0.40 PHI=0.80
+ TOX=4.1n CGSO=2.4e-10 CGDO=2.4e-10
+ TNOM=27 TCV=-0.9m BEX=-1.5
+ AVT=3.5m ABETA=0.010

.model PCH PMOS
+ VTO=-0.45 KP=86u LAMBDA=0.10 GAMMA=0.45 PHI=0.85
+ TOX=4.1n CGSO=2.6e-10 CGDO=2.6e-10
+ TNOM=27 TCV=-0.9m BEX=-1.5
+ AVT=4.2m ABETA=0.012
